      ":question/id": "051effd0-f0ca-56ac-80f4-c13fb6384d81",
      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-1442",
      ":question/problem": "In the year $2009$, there were approximately $4120$ crimes in a particular city. The police department then promised a $3.81 \\mathrm{\\% }$ annual *decrease* in crime, continuously compounded. According to this model, how many crimes occurred in $2016$? Round your answer to the nearest integer.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question.",
      ":question/requires-calculator": true,
      ":question/worked-solution": "The continuously compounded growth equation is $P=P_0e^{rt}$. Here $P_0=4120$, $r=-0.0381$ per year, and $t=2016-2009=7$ years. Substitute:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP &= 4120e^{(-0.0381)(7)} \\\\\n&= 4120e^{-0.2667} \\\\\n&\\approx 3155.5196.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRounding to the nearest integer gives approximately $3156$ crimes in $2016$."
    },
