      ":question/id": "c9077fb0-4ca3-538c-9a63-2f4162f39301",
      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-1445",
      ":question/problem": "In medieval times, there were $9830$ people living in a city struck by a plague. If the disease resulted in a daily *decrease* in the population at a continuously compounded rate of $18 \\mathrm{\\% } ,$ what was the city's population after $2$ weeks? Round your answer to the nearest integer.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question.",
      ":question/requires-calculator": true,
      ":question/worked-solution": "The continuously compounded growth equation is $P=P_0e^{rt}$. Here $P_0=9830$ and $r=-0.18$ per day. Convert $2$ weeks to $t=14$ days, then substitute:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP &= 9830e^{(-0.18)(14)} \\\\\n&= 9830e^{-2.52} \\\\\n&\\approx 790.9179.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRounding to the nearest integer gives approximately $791$ people."
    },
