      ":question/id": "3baaacd5-ce43-59a2-b728-fb3d5a7a28e0",
      ":question/problem": "In the year $2014$, there were approximately $8990$ crimes in a particular city. The police department then promised a $4.7\\%$ annual *decrease* in crime, continuously compounded. According to this model, how many crimes occurred in $2022$? Round your answer to the nearest integer.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question.",
      ":question/requires-calculator": true,
      ":question/worked-solution": "The continuously compounded growth equation is $P=P_0e^{rt}$. The initial amount is $P_0=8990$. Since the amount decreases, the signed decimal rate is $r=-4.7/100=-0.047$. The elapsed time is $t=2022-2014=8$ years.\n\nSubstitute these values and round only the final amount:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP &= P_0e^{rt} \\\\\n&= 8990e^{(-0.047)(8)} \\\\\n&= 8990e^{-0.376} \\\\\n&= 8990(0.6866023\\ldots) \\\\\n&\\approx 6173\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to this model, approximately $6173$ crimes occurred in $2022$."
    },
