      ":question/id": "3cb6a6d9-d90c-5424-8cd2-1b6b6fde595b",
      ":question/problem": "In medieval times, there were $9660$ people living in a city struck by a plague. If the disease resulted in a daily *decrease* in the population at a continuously compounded rate of $5.2\\%$, what was the city's population after $3$ weeks? Round your answer to the nearest integer.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question.",
      ":question/requires-calculator": true,
      ":question/worked-solution": "The continuously compounded growth equation is $P=P_0e^{rt}$. The initial amount is $P_0=9660$. Since the amount decreases, the signed decimal rate is $r=-5.2/100=-0.052$. The rate is daily, so convert the duration to days: $t=3\\times 7=21$ days.\n\nSubstitute these values and round only the final amount:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP &= P_0e^{rt} \\\\\n&= 9660e^{(-0.052)(21)} \\\\\n&= 9660e^{-1.092} \\\\\n&= 9660(0.3355447\\ldots) \\\\\n&\\approx 3241\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAfter $3$ weeks, the population was approximately $3241$ people."
    },
