      ":question/id": "894ca8fd-a74a-585e-ad54-7c29860968cb",
      ":question/problem": "In the year $2006$, there were approximately $19180$ crimes in a particular city. The police department then promised a $5.1\\%$ annual *decrease* in crime, continuously compounded. According to this model, how many crimes occurred in $2008$? Round your answer to the nearest integer.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question.",
      ":question/requires-calculator": true,
      ":question/worked-solution": "The continuously compounded growth equation is $P=P_0e^{rt}$. The initial amount is $P_0=19180$. Since the amount decreases, the signed decimal rate is $r=-5.1/100=-0.051$. The elapsed time is $t=2008-2006=2$ years.\n\nSubstitute these values and round only the final amount:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP &= P_0e^{rt} \\\\\n&= 19180e^{(-0.051)(2)} \\\\\n&= 19180e^{-0.102} \\\\\n&= 19180(0.9030295\\ldots) \\\\\n&\\approx 17320\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to this model, approximately $17320$ crimes occurred in $2008$."
    },
