      ":question/id": "b430f767-4592-541a-b047-59097359d724",
      ":question/problem": "In the year $1996$, there were approximately $6500$ crimes in a particular city. The police department then promised a $4.2\\%$ annual *decrease* in crime, continuously compounded. According to this model, how many crimes occurred in $2004$? Round your answer to the nearest integer.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question.",
      ":question/requires-calculator": true,
      ":question/worked-solution": "The continuously compounded growth equation is $P=P_0e^{rt}$. The initial amount is $P_0=6500$. Since the amount decreases, the signed decimal rate is $r=-4.2/100=-0.042$. The elapsed time is $t=2004-1996=8$ years.\n\nSubstitute these values and round only the final amount:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP &= P_0e^{rt} \\\\\n&= 6500e^{(-0.042)(8)} \\\\\n&= 6500e^{-0.336} \\\\\n&= 6500(0.7146231\\ldots) \\\\\n&\\approx 4645\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to this model, approximately $4645$ crimes occurred in $2004$."
    },
